<title>USA: Apple reports third-quarter loss.</title>
<headline>Apple reports third-quarter loss.</headline>
<dateline>PALO ALTO, Calif. 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Apple Computer Inc. reported another quarterly loss on Wednesday, as sales of its flagship Macintosh line continued its downward spiral.</p>
<p>The Cupertino, Calif.-based computer maker lost $56 million, or 44 cents a share, in its fiscal third quarter ended in June, marking the third straight quarterly loss for Apple and the sixth time in the last seven quarters Apple has been in the red. Revenues fell to $1.7 billion from $2.2 billion in the year-ago period, when Apple posted a loss of $32 million, or 26 cents a share.</p>
</text>
